# Service worker headers, for a host that serves the web app's public/ folder
# from disk.
#
# This is a block, not a file to upload. An operator appends it ONCE to the
# .htaccess the host already keeps in the web app's document root, below the
# host's own managed blocks. It never replaces that file: the host's blocks
# are what start the app, and the deploy refuses a bundle that carries a
# public/.htaccess of its own for that reason.
#
# It exists because next.config.js sets these two headers for /sw.js only on
# requests that reach the Next.js process. Where the web server answers a file
# under public/ itself, that rule never runs, and this block is what keeps the
# worker uncached and confined to same-origin scripts (ADR 0127).
#
# Keep both values in step with next.config.js; `yarn staging-web:test` fails
# when they differ. Staging's deploy fails its probe when /sw.js comes back
# without them.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  <Files "sw.js">
    Header set Cache-Control "no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate"
    Header set Content-Security-Policy "default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'"
  </Files>
</IfModule>
